"Invalid scaling of plane\n");
```
```c
drm_dbg_kms(plane_state->crtc->dev,
"Plane must cover entire CRTC\n");
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the logging attempts to access `plane_state->crtc->dev` when the `drm_device` cannot be found in the `crtc`, leading to incorrect logging behavior and potential errors when updating the plane state of a disabled CRTC.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
drm_dbg_kms(plane_state->plane->dev,
"Cannot update plane of a disabled CRTC.\n");
```
```c
drm_dbg_kms(plane_state->plane->dev,
"Invalid scaling of plane\n");
```
```c
drm_dbg_kms(plane_state->plane->dev,
"Plane must cover entire CRTC\n");
```
Reason:
The fix changes the logging to reference `plane_state->plane->dev` instead of `plane_state->crtc->dev`, ensuring that the correct device context is used, which prevents errors when the `drm_device` is not found in the `crtc`.


